user_prompt_template:
TUTORIAL REQUEST: {topic}
SKILL LEVEL: {skill_level}
TUTORIAL TYPE: {tutorial_type}
STACK / LANGUAGE / FRAMEWORK: {stack}
PLATFORM / ENVIRONMENT: {platform}
DESIRED DEPTH: {depth}
INCLUDE CODE SNIPPETS: {include_code}
OUTPUT STYLE: {output_style}
CONSTRAINTS (time budget, preferred tools, things to avoid): {constraints}
AUDIENCE: {audience}
TONE: {tone}
ADDITIONAL CONTEXT: {context}

Frame a complete tutorial for this request. Every field is mandatory. Be specific to this exact topic, stack, and skill level — no generic outlines, no placeholder values, no output that could apply to a different tutorial.

Scope the number of modules to the requested depth: 3–4 modules for 'quick', 4–6 for 'standard', 6–8 for 'deep-dive'.

Before writing, ask yourself: could any of these fields apply to a completely different tutorial? If yes, rewrite until they cannot.

Return ONLY the following JSON object. No prose. No markdown. No code fences.

{{
  "system_name": "Specific tutorial title that promises a concrete outcome — names the thing built or mastered and the stack used",
  "topic": "The tutorial request exactly as provided",
  "operating_premise": "One sentence naming the specific difficulty or confusion this tutorial resolves — the real reason a structured walkthrough is needed for this exact topic",
  "system_objective": "One sentence: the verifiable end state when the learner finishes. Name the artifact produced and how to confirm it works (command output, URL, observable behavior).",
  "time_horizon": "Realistic completion estimate for this skill level — e.g. '2–3 hours hands-on', '45 minutes including deploy', 'a weekend project in 4 sessions'",
  "control_domains": [
    {{
      "id": "domain-01",
      "name": "Specific module name with its concrete deliverable — could not apply to a different tutorial",
      "purpose": "What the learner builds or masters in this module and why it comes at this point in the sequence",
      "scope_in": ["Specific tasks, files, and commands covered in this module"],
      "scope_out": ["Specific related tasks explicitly deferred or excluded — name where they are covered instead, if anywhere"],
      "primary_outputs": ["Tangible outputs: named files created, features working, commands succeeding, checks passing"]
    }}
  ],
  "key_roles": [
    {{
      "role": "Tool / framework / service name with version where relevant",
      "responsibility": "What this tool does in THIS tutorial — be specific about its job in the build",
      "authority_level": "required | recommended | optional | alternative"
    }}
  ],
  "critical_milestones": [
    {{
      "milestone": "Specific checkpoint name — e.g. 'Dev server renders the scaffold'",
      "description": "What it means to reach this checkpoint and the exact verification — command run, output seen, behavior observed",
      "sequence": 1
    }}
  ],
  "success_criteria": ["Specific, verifiable outcome — a command that succeeds, output that appears, or behavior observable in the browser/terminal"],
  "failure_modes": ["Specific blocker: the mistake, the observable symptom (exact error message where possible), and where in the tutorial it bites"],
  "operating_constraints": ["Concrete prerequisites and environment requirements — installed tools with versions, accounts needed, OS assumptions, API keys, prior knowledge assumed"]
}}
